      "extract": "A popular axiomatization of the notion of TQFT was proposed by Micheal Atiyah \\cite{A88}, who was inspired by a similar definition of Graeme Segal \\cite{S88} for the concept of a Conformal Field Theory (CFT for short). Paraphrasing Atiyah, a TQFT in dimension 3 can be defined as a symmetric monoidal functor from a category of 3-dimensional cobordisms to the category of vector spaces. In this definition, cobordism",
